dV1","type":"object"},"TryCatchCatchBodyV1":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The recovery path for a caught document.\n\nMANDATORY and MUST terminate: a caught document that reaches no terminal is\na document the process silently drops. The terminal set is the recovery\nvocabulary \u2014 stop the document, raise it as an explicit failure, or stage it\nfor a downstream handler.\n\nSteps may be empty (a bare terminal is a meaningful recovery), but a bare\n``stop`` with no work at all is rejected: it recovers nothing.","properties":{"steps":{"items":{"discriminator":{"mapping":{"cache_get":"#/$defs/CacheGetNodeV1","cache_put":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1","cache_remove":"#/$defs/CacheRemoveNodeV1","connector_call":"#/$defs/ConnectorCallNodeV1","document_cache_retrieve":"#/$defs/DocumentCacheRetrieveNodeV1","map_ref":"#/$defs/MapRefNodeV1","message":"#/$defs/MessageNodeV1","set_ddp":"#/$defs/SetDdpNodeV1","set_dpp":"#/$defs/SetDppNodeV1"},"propertyName":"kind"},"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/MessageNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/MapRefNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/DocumentCacheRetrieveNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CacheGetNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CacheRemoveNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/SetDdpNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/SetDppNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/ConnectorCallNodeV1"}]},"title":"Steps","type":"array"},"terminal":{"discriminator":{"mapping":{"cache_put":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1","exception":"#/$defs/ExceptionNodeV1","stop":"#/$defs/StopNodeV1"},"propertyName":"kind"},"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/StopNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/ExceptionNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1"}],"title":"Terminal"}},"required":["terminal"],"title":"TryCatchCatchBodyV1","type":"object"},"TryCatchNodeV1":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Scoped error handling with bounded retry (#142, M12.7).\n\nPlacement is part of the contract, because scope is not a free-form label \u2014\neach value names a placement the compiler has a verified shape for:\n\n* ``process`` is the sole root step, and its protected path begins with the\n  call that produces the flow's documents;\n* ``connector`` is the terminal step of a call sequence, and protects exactly\n  one downstream call plus the property steps that prepare it.\n\nNothing may follow a Try/Catch: both paths terminate independently and there\nis no join.\n\nRetry is bounded and additionally CONSTRAINED BY SAFETY, not just by range: a\npositive count is rejected when the protected region would re-run the flow's\ndocument source, and when a retried call writes without registry-backed\nreplay safety. Those checks run before anything is emitted.","properties":{"catch_body":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TryCatchCatchBodyV1"},"kind":{"const":"try_catch","title":"Kind","type":"string"},"label":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null,"title":"Label"},"retry":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/RetryPolicyV1"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"scope":{"enum":["process","connector"],"title":"Scope","type":"string"},"try_body":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TryCatchTryBodyV1"}},"required":["kind","scope","try_body","catch_body"],"title":"TryCatchNodeV1","type":"object"},"TryCatchTryBodyV1":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The protected path.\n\nTerminates on a plain ``stop`` only. An ``exception`` here would be caught by\nthis very scope's own recovery path, and no evidence covers that loop; a\nstaging ``cache_put`` terminal is a recovery-path shape, not a success one.","properties":{"steps":{"items":{"discriminator":{"mapping":{"cache_get":"#/$defs/CacheGetNodeV1","cache_put":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1","cache_remove":"#/$defs/CacheRemoveNodeV1","connector_call":"#/$defs/ConnectorCallNodeV1","document_cache_retrieve":"#/$defs/DocumentCacheRetrieveNodeV1","map_ref":"#/$defs/MapRefNodeV1","message":"#/$defs/MessageNodeV1","set_ddp":"#/$defs/SetDdpNodeV1","set_dpp":"#/$defs/SetDppNodeV1"},"propertyName":"kind"},"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/MessageNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/MapRefNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CachePutNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/DocumentCacheRetrieveNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CacheGetNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/CacheRemoveNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/SetDdpNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/SetDppNodeV1"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/ConnectorCallNodeV1"}]},"minItems":1,"title":"Steps","type":"array"},"terminal":{"discriminator":{"mapping":{"stop":"#/$defs/StopNodeV1"},"propertyName":"kind"},"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/$defs/StopNodeV1"}],"title":"Terminal"}},"required":["steps","terminal"],"title":"TryCatchTryBodyV1","type":"object"},"VerifiedActionIdempotencyV1":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The action itself is idempotent, as classified by the connector registry.\n\nCarries no payload: the claim is entirely about the resolved action, which the\ncompiler already knows. Authoring it is an acknowledgement, not an assertion\nthe compiler trusts.","properties":{"kind":{"const":"verified_action","title":"Kind","type":"string"}},"required":["kind"],"title":"VerifiedActionIdempotencyV1","type":"object"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The semantic root: exactly one per authored process (ADR-001 \u00a73).","properties":{"body":{"$ref":"#/$defs/SequenceNodeV1"},"version":{"const":"1","title":"Version","type":"string"}},"required":["version","body"],"title":"ProcessIRV1","type":"object"}